11:T603,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is a myopia management consultation?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A specialist consultation for children and young people with progressing short-sightedness, using evidence-based treatments to slow myopia progression."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does a myopia management consultation take?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A myopia management consultation typically takes 30–45 minutes for the initial consultation."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does a myopia management consultation cost?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"£50–£150 for the initial consultation. Ongoing treatment costs vary: specialist spectacle lenses £200–£400, myopia control contact lenses £30–£60 per month, ortho-k lenses £400–£800 for the first year. Not funded by the NHS"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How often should I have a myopia management consultation?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Review appointments every 6 months during active treatment to monitor progression and adjust the management plan"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is a myopia management consultation available on the NHS?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A myopia management consultation is not routinely funded by the NHS and is typically available as a private service. Some opticians may include elements of this test within a standard NHS-funded sight test where clinically indicated."}}]}5:[["$","$L10",null,{}],["$","main",null,{"className":"flex-1","children":[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"MedicalWebPage\",\"name\":\"Myopia Management Consultation\",\"description\":\"A specialist consultation for children and young people with progressing short-sightedness, using evidence-based treatments to slow myopia progression.\",\"url\":\"https://www.eyetes